# Model artifacts
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.bin
!tests/**/*.pt          # allow test fixtures
checkpoints/
runs/
logs/
wandb/
# Local downloads of the merged/converted model — these are multi-GB
# artifacts (9.7GB / 500MB+ each), never source, and were caught NOT being
# excluded by the patterns above (no directory-name match, and *.bin didn't
# exist yet) — a plain `git add .` would have staged all of it.
vasudha-model/
vasudha/checkpoint-*/
local_weights.bin

# Triton cache
.triton/
triton_cache/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_meta

# Data
data/
datasets/
# Keep the Python package named ``vasudha.datasets``; the broad ``datasets/``
# rule above is for downloaded Hugging Face data, not source code.
!vasudha/datasets/
!vasudha/datasets/*.py
*.jsonl
*.json.gz
*.parquet

# GGUF
*.gguf
*.ggml

# HuggingFace cache (large)
.cache/
huggingface/

# Build artifacts
*.o
*.a
*.lib

# Packaged desktop builds.
#
# `dist/` and `build/` are covered by the Python rules near the top, but
# PyInstaller cannot clean dist/Vasudha while any shell has it as a working
# directory, so builds get redirected to dist_build/. That is 212 MB of
# executable and bundled DLLs, and a plain `git add -A` was measured staging
# 1523 files / 129 MB of it. Release binaries belong on a GitHub release, not
# in the history, where they can never be removed.
dist_build/
*.zip

# Model source config is committed as a template with an empty url; the copy
# carrying the real download link is written by scripts/publish_model.py.
# (model_source.json itself IS tracked — this note is here so nobody adds it.)

# Profiling
*.prof
*.lprof
